'''Pradip Chatterjee''' (born 15 December 1950) is a founder member of the Bengali band [[Moheener Ghoraguli]]. He is the younger brother of [[Gautam Chatterjee]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Song of the stallion |url=http://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/Kolkata-/Song-of-the-stallion/articleshow/4681928.cms |work=The Times of India |date=21 June 2009}}</ref> He was also a theatre person, filmmaker and ethnographer.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Bapi-da of Mohiner Ghoraguli loses battle to cancer |url=https://www.telegraphindia.com/my-kolkata/news/bapi-da-of-mohiner-ghoraguli-loses-battle-to-cancer/cid/1947601 |access-date=2023-08-27 |work=The Telegraph}}</ref>

Also known as ''Bula'', Chatterjee is a flautist and vocalist.

==Career==
[[File:MoheenerGhoraguli-group.jpg|thumb|right|280px|[[Moheener Ghoraguli]] in concert at [[Rabindra Sadan]], 1979, left to right: Raja Banerjee, Pradip Chatterjee, Tapas Das, Pranab Sengupta, [[Gautam Chattopadhyay]] and [[Ranjon Ghoshal]].]]
An engineering graduate from the [[Indian Institute of Engineering Science and Technology, Shibpur]], which was then affiliated with the [[University of Calcutta]], he joined the Calcutta engineering firm M.N. Dastur & Company (P) Ltd, after the break-up of Moheener Ghoraguli.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Last founding member of Moheener Ghoraguli Tapas Bapi Das dies |url=https://www.newagebd.net/article/205151/last-founding-member-of-moheener-ghoraguli-tapas-bapi-das-dies |access-date=2023-08-27 |work=New Age |language=en}}</ref>

He resides in Kolkata, with his wife Sharmistha, daughter Anka and son Ritoban.

